\ge2,\\;a+b\\ge n-k+2 .\\tag{2}\n\\]\n\nThe number of points that satisfy (2) is exactly \\(k\\).  \nIndeed, for each integer \\(s\\) with \\(n-k+2\\le s\\le n+1\\) there is precisely one pair \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a,b\\ge2\\) and \\(a+b=s\\); the values of \\(s\\) give \\(k\\) distinct points.  \nDenote this uncovered set by  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal U=\\{(a_1,b_1),\\dots ,(a_k,b_k)\\}.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n#### 2.3  Sunny lines covering the remaining points  \n\nFor the \\(j\\)-th point \\((a_j,b_j)\\in\\mathcal U\\) draw the line  \n\n\\[\nM_j:\\;\\text{through }(a_j,b_j)\\text{ and }(0,-j).\n\\]\n\nIts slope is  \n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{slope}(M_j)=\\frac{b_j-(-j)}{a_j-0}= \\frac{b_j+j}{a_j}>0 .\n\\]\n\nHence \\(\\operatorname{slope}(M_j)\\) is different from \\(0\\), from \\(\\infty\\) (the line is not vertical because \\(a_j>0\\)), and from \\(-1\\).  \nThus each \\(M_j\\) is a sunny line.\n\nThe second point on the \\(x\\)-axis is different for each \\(j\\); therefore the \\(k\\) lines \\(M_1,\\dots ,M_k\\) are distinct.\n\n---\n\n#### 2.4  Counting the lines  \n\nThe total family of lines is  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal L_k:=\\mathcal N\\cup\\{M_1,\\dots ,M_k\\}.\n\\]\n\nIts cardinality is  \n\n\\[\n|\\mathcal L_k|\n=2\\;(\\text{vertical, horizontal})\n+(n-2-k)\\;(\\text{slope }-1)\n+k\\;(\\text{sunny})\n=n .\n\\]\n\nExactly \\(k\\) of them (the \\(M_j\\)’s) are sunny, the remaining \\(n-k\\) are non‑sunny.  \nBy construction every point of \\(\\mathcal P_n\\) lies on at least one line of \\(\\mathcal L_k\\).\n\nThus for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) a suitable configuration exists.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  Conclusion\n\nThe necessary condition (1) shows that no configuration can have \\(k\\ge n-1\\).  \nThe construction of §2 shows that every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) is attainable.\n\nHence the set of all non‑negative integers \\(k\\) for which the required configuration exists is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-2\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
