ontains the unique point \\((i,\\,n+1-i)\\) that no other \\(\\ell_j\\) contains.\n\nBy construction \\(\\mathcal L_k\\) covers every point of \\(S_n\\) and contains precisely the \\(k\\) sunny lines \\(\\ell_1,\\dots ,\\ell_k\\).  Hence for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) a required configuration exists.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n#### 6.  Final conclusion  \n\nLemma 2 shows that a configuration with \\(k=n-1\\) or \\(k=n\\) sunny lines cannot exist.  \nLemma 3 together with the replacement procedure above shows that for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) a configuration does exist.\n\nTherefore the set of all non‑negative integers \\(k\\) for which the problem’s requirements can be met is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-2\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
