hecked directly and also fail). Therefore a covering with exactly one non‑sunny line cannot exist, and \\(k=n-1\\) is impossible.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5.  Final conclusion\n\nThe construction of Section 1 shows that every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) can be realised.  \nSections 2–4 prove that no configuration can have \\(k\\ge n-1\\).  \n\nConsequently, for a given integer \\(n\\ge3\\) the set of admissible numbers of sunny lines is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-2\\}}.\n\\]"
