ting (there are only \\(n\\) lines).\n\n---\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\nThe solution correctly identifies the combinatorial constraints and derives the necessary inequality \\(P\\le s^{2}\\). The algebraic manipulation is sound. However, two essential justification gaps remain:\n\n1. **Equating the number of sunny lines with the number of non\u2011diagonal lines** without proving that all non\u2011diagonal lines can be chosen to avoid horizontal and vertical slopes.\n\n2. **Providing a rigorous construction** of the \\(s\\) sunny (non\u2011diagonal) lines that simultaneously cover all required points while remaining distinct and of admissible slope.\n\nBecause these gaps are not filled, the solution does not meet the rigorous standards expected for an IMO\u2011level proof."

